---
/**
 * krone-iot.astro — KRONE IoT Telemetry Architecture Case Study
 * Deep Architectural Breakdown · Production Systems Metrics
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import FloatingNav from '../../components/nav/FloatingNav';
import ReadingProgress from '../../components/ui/ReadingProgress';
import Footer from '../../components/contact/Footer.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="KRONE IoT Telemetry Case Study | Naveen Bishnoi" 
  description="Architectural deep-dive: Ingesting 50,000+ agricultural machines at sub-200ms latency with edge Kafka streams, offline WAL buffers, and predictive AI."
>
  <ReadingProgress client:load />
  <FloatingNav client:load slot="header" />

  <div class="w-full min-h-screen bg-[var(--color-canvas)] pt-32 sm:pt-40 pb-24 text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">
    <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-12">
      
      {/* Return Link */}
      <a
        href="/projects"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline mb-8 cursor-pointer"
      >
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18" />
        </svg>
        <span>Back to Projects Gallery</span>
      </a>

      <header class="mb-12 md:mb-16">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6 md:mb-8">
          <span class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 font-mono text-sm tracking-widest uppercase font-bold">Case Study 01</span>
          <div class="h-px bg-black/[0.08] dark:bg-white/10 flex-1"></div>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl font-black tracking-tight leading-tight mb-6 md:mb-8 text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">
          KRONE IoT Telemetry Engine
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] font-normal leading-relaxed">
          Predictive Analytics &amp; Edge Fleet Management architecture capable of ingesting high-throughput sensor telemetry globally from 50,000+ heavy harvesters and balers.
        </p>
      </header>

      {/* Hero Visual Image Banner */}
      <div class="relative w-full rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-12 border border-black/[0.08] dark:border-white/15 shadow-[0_16px_48px_rgba(0,0,0,0.15)] bg-slate-900">
        <img
          src="/images/krone-telematics.jpg"
          alt="KRONE Agricultural Telematics Cockpit"
          class="w-full h-auto object-cover max-h-[460px]"
        />
        <div class="absolute bottom-3 left-3 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-black/70 backdrop-blur-md border border-white/20 text-white text-xs font-mono">
          CAN-Bus Ingestion Runtime · 50Hz Real-Time Stream
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-10 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] mb-4 tracking-tight">1. The Problem</h2>
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">
            Managing a global fleet of agricultural machinery requires real-time insight into hardware health, location, and yield data. Traditional polling architectures were failing under the load of thousands of simultaneous socket connections, resulting in dropped telemetry packets and delayed predictive maintenance alerts across remote farming fields.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] mb-4 tracking-tight">2. Distributed Architecture</h2>
          <div class="w-full p-6 sm:p-8 bg-[#0D111A] border border-white/10 rounded-2xl mb-6 font-mono text-xs sm:text-sm overflow-x-auto text-zinc-200 shadow-inner">
            <pre>
[ Machinery Fleet (50k+ Harvesters) ] --&gt; ISO 11783 CAN-Bus --&gt; [ Edge Ingestion Gateway ]
                                                                       |
                                                           [ Offline WAL Disk Ring (4GB) ]
                                                                       |
                                                           [ Apache Kafka Broker Cluster ]
                                                             /                       \
                                         [ Redis Real-Time Cache ]         [ TimescaleDB Persistent ]
                                                    |                                    |
                                          [ Operator Telematics UI ]           [ Predictive Failure Engine ]
            </pre>
          </div>
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg leading-relaxed font-normal">
            To solve the throughput bottleneck, we shifted to an event-driven edge-cloud hybrid architecture. <strong>FastAPI &amp; C++ edge daemon</strong> handle socket connections asynchronously, spooling telemetry payloads into an <strong>Apache Kafka</strong> cluster. When machines lose cellular connectivity in rural farmlands, local write-ahead logs (WAL) preserve data until handshake restoration.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] mb-4 tracking-tight">3. Empirical Impact &amp; Results</h2>
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-4">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 text-base sm:text-lg">
              <span class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0">→</span>
              <span><strong>Scaled Ingestion:</strong> Grew from 1,000 to 50,000+ concurrent machines without packet loss.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 text-base sm:text-lg">
              <span class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0">→</span>
              <span><strong>Latency Slashed:</strong> Reduced data pipeline processing latency from 4 seconds to under 200ms.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-4 text-base sm:text-lg">
              <span class="text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400 font-bold shrink-0">→</span>
              <span><strong>Uptime Boost:</strong> Predictive AI vibration diagnostics reduced average seasonal hardware downtime by 24%.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>
    </article>
  </div>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
